Sofia (Eng): hey team — noticed my June paycheck withheld Swiss income tax even though I was on a US-taxed short-term assignment. net pay is much lower than expected :confused;
Ana (Payroll): thanks for flagging — can you drop the payslip (pdf) and the date range for the assignment? we need the payroll id and work_location on the record.;
Sofia (Eng): attached (payslip_jun.pdf) — assignment dates 2024-05-20 to 2024-06-30. payroll id 0045123. employer processed in CH payroll cluster.;
Ana (Payroll): looking. i can see YTD Swiss withholding code CH-TAX applied for Jun run. Payroll Bot shows work_location=CH and tax_residency=US in employee record (weird combo). @miguel could this be a treaty & withholding flags issue?;
Miguel (Tax): yep — short-term business traveler should be US-taxable if <183 days and employer didn't have a Swiss permanent establishment; there is a US-Switzerland treaty position for short visits. we should: 1) reverse the Swiss withholding for June, 2) issue a refund (net adjustment) or retro pay, and 3) ensure year-to-date US withholding and FICA are correct. we may need to amend Swiss payroll records so they don't issue a Lohnsteuerbescheinigung incorrectly.;
Jordan (People Ops): priority please — employee is short on cash. what's fastest: a cash refund now and payroll correction next month?;
Ana (Payroll): fastest is manual gross-up/adjustment in July run to refund net tax withheld in June while doing the retro tax correction in our system. i can do a manual credit now but need approval from Tax for the treaty justification, and Finance to code GL. @miguel ok to approve treaty note?;
Miguel (Tax): approved — treaty position documented. we'll provide a short memo for Finance. two followups: A) determine whether Swiss authorities expect an employer correction (Lohnsteuer reporting) — might require filing an adjusted wage statement; B) determine if we should issue a Form W-2 correction (if US withholding changed materially).;
Ana (Payroll): action items for payroll (internal):;
- locate payroll run: CH_CLUSTER 2024-06;
- create adjustment: tax_reversal_CH code CH-REV, amount CHF 2,180.45 (gross withheld);
- create refund line: paycode MANUAL_REFUND, currency CHF -> convert to USD at 2024-06-30 rate;
- flag employee record: tax_resolution=SWISS_REVERSAL_2024-06;
Ana (Payroll): i'll schedule the manual refund in tomorrow's off-cycle run. Finance, please confirm GL mapping for CH reversals (will post in #finance later).;
Payroll Bot: Off-cycle pay run queued: offcycle-20240702-ana (ETA 24h) — tickets: PAY-7321.;
Sofia (Eng): thanks. do i need to file anything on my side with Swiss authorities?;
Miguel (Tax): no for the employee — employer handles withholding corrections. but if Swiss authorities later demand a reclaim, they might ask the employee for proof of short stay; keep travel docs and assignment memo. we'll prepare an employee letter you can present.;
Jordan (People Ops): wrinkle: if we reverse CH withholding, US withholding and FICA should be recalculated — payroll to confirm YTD US tax withholding increases vs original. if W-2 changes, we need to evaluate W-2c.;
Ana (Payroll): confirmed — after refund we'll run a YTD recalc and if federal/state comps changed we'll issue a corrected W-2 (W-2c) in coordination with Payroll Tax. Estimated timeline: refund (immediate), YTD recalc + W-2 decision within 10 business days, Swiss wage statement correction within 20 business days pending local tax advisor.;
Miguel (Tax): i'll draft the treaty memo and the employee letter today. cc @jordan for approvals.;
Jordan (People Ops): approved. please include one-line note for People Ops that this was a payroll mapping issue (work_location flag set to CH cluster) so we can update the onboarding checklist.;
Ana (Payroll): action completed: created PAY-7321, refund queued, flagged record tax_resolution=SWISS_REVERSAL_2024-06. will post confirmation when off-cycle posts.;
Payroll Bot: Off-cycle pay completed: offcycle-20240702-ana — refund posted CHF->USD 2,180.45 -> $2,377.12, transaction id TX-998211.;
Sofia (Eng): refund hit my account, thank you! :purple_heart: any note about future relocations so this doesn't repeat?;
Miguel (Tax): short checklist for future: set tax_residency correctly on day 1; if assignment <183 days set treaty_exemption=true; use payroll flag employer_PE=false unless legal confirms otherwise. i'll attach checklist to the employee travel policy doc.;
Jordan (People Ops): we'll add a step to the relocation/hotdesk doc: confirm "tax_residency" vs "work_location" with Mobility before first payroll run.;
Ana (Payroll): closing loop — will run YTD recalc next Tue and confirm if W-2c required. if W-2c needed we'll notify employee and file promptly.;
Sofia (Eng): great — appreciate the quick turnaround. saved my rent :relieved:
